Allows to customize the partitioning schemas of your servers (available on some offers and OSs).

USAGE:
  scw baremetal partitioning-schemas <command>

AVAILABLE COMMANDS:
  get-default Get default partitioning schema
  validate    Validate client partitioning schema

FLAGS:
  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for partitioning-schemas
      --list-sub-commands[=true|false]   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta[=true|false]         Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string             The path to the config file
  -D, --debug[=true|false]        Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers[=true|false]   Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string             Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string            The config profile to use

Use "scw baremetal partitioning-schemas [command] --help" for more information about a command.
